{
    "UniqueID": "hw_fleas",
    "//Fleas": "The first Harsh Wilds AFFLICTION: one VISIBLE GameStat whose icon statuses do the harm (Documentation/Research/HarshWilds/afflictions.md sections 1.7 and 2.3, the skeleton DECISION and the first fleas DECISION). The key set is exactly HerbsAndFungi/GameStat/HF_HerbalTonic.json's. Visibility 0 (VisibleWithStatus) with an icon on every status is how vanilla BugBites, Parasites and Rash are seen: InGameStat.FindFirstVisibleStatus shows the first current status that has an Icon, so a status without one is invisible, and at 0 (no status in range) nothing shows because the default status is only built for AlwaysVisible or pinned stats (GameManager status update). VisibleInDetailedList false and NO detailed-tab entry: a StatListTab is scene-scoped and GameSourceModify cannot reach it (CLAUDE.md GameSourceModify), and the status strip is all an affliction needs. BaseRatePerTick HW_FLEAS_RATE = 0: fleas never leave on their own, so a cure matters (vanilla Parasites is rate 0 too). Every write to this stat is a PERMANENT base write clamped on write (GameManager.ChangeStatValue): the four sources (SelfTriggeredAction/Tgr_HW_FleasBedLeaf, Tgr_HW_FleasBedSkin, Tgr_HW_FleasDirty, Tgr_HW_FleasCompanion) each add HW_FLEAS_PER_INFEST = 96 (one band) only when their roll picks the Fleas collection; the cures subtract (Tgr_HW_FleasWash -24 every 24 ticks while clean, Tgr_HW_FleasBogMyrtle and Tgr_HW_FleasJuniper -4 a tick while vanilla's repellent effect lasts, CardData/Item/hw_herbal_wash -144, or -288 with a herb), and Tgr_HW_FleasSwitchOff clears it while the [Threats] FleasAndLice switch is off. Every write is a multiple of 4, so the values it can land on are the multiples of 4 from 0 to the cap; every trigger on it starts at 1 and is open at the top, so no trigger edge sits on a landing value or on the cap (Development_Tools/Tests/HarshWilds-Afflictions.Tests.ps1 [clamp-own]). No perk writes it (no StartingStatModifiers anywhere in the mod). Status costs are GLOBAL modifiers, clamped when read, and touch only vanilla Comfort (value) and Stress (rate): Comfort HW_FLEAS_COMFORT_1..3 = -10, -25, -40 (range -100..100, so it cannot pin), Stress HW_FLEAS_STRESS_1..3 = +0.25, +0.5, +1.0 a tick, half of vanilla Rash's because Rash heals itself and this does not. Against vanilla Stress's own base rate -0.25 and its own status rates (-0.5 from 145, -1.0 from 193) band 1 only stops stress easing, band 2 settles near 145 and band 3 near 193, so fleas alone never pin Stress at 240, where vanilla Tgr_Anxiety fires (the gate's [clamp-rate] recomputes that from the export). Icons are vanilla sprite names checked against VanillaSprites.txt: BugBites_Old for the first two bands and the default, Bugs_Old for the third. Every number here is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER (HW_FLEAS_*), session-inferred and unmeasured against play, never balanced.",
    "GameName": {
